{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "itop",
  "description": "The four default CI classes, with the interface classes read once up front and joined by owner id. Proves version and json_data travel as form fields while the credential stays in an Authorization header - iTop's auth_user and auth_pwd fields belong to the 'url' login type, which is absent from the shipped allowed_login_types default; that PhysicalInterface and LogicalInterface are read directly instead of through a *_list link set the vendor docs warn against; that a managementip becomes an interface only when no modelled interface already carries it; that an unparseable macaddress is dropped rather than passed through; that a loopback interface yields no address; and that a move2production date in the future is clamped rather than dropping the whole record.",
